    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for the Austin Waves highlights two standout plays: **Jacob Wilson** (74.08) and **Gunnar Henderson** (73.28), who anchor the lineup with the highest efficiency scores. **Jacob Wilson** benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Cody Bradford (5.29 xERA), where a +10% park factor and +19% SP skill advantage propel him into elite territory. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** faces the tougher Freddy Peralta, but he remains a must-start due to a +14% dynamic platoon edge and a +2% boost from Peralta\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a high-probability opportunity to secure the stolen bases we prioritize for our 5x5 standing. **Jackson Merrill** also provides strong secondary value at 69.57, leveraging a favorable +13% platoon split against Tanner Bibee.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Heliot Ramos** (45.00), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Dominic Smith** and **Coby Mayo**. While **Heliot Ramos** carried a solid projection, he was negatively impacted by the difficult matchup against Dylan Cease (2.95 xERA), whose elite skill set suppressed the scoring potential of our outfield depth. We opted to prioritize the platoon advantages of **Dominic Smith** and the specific, albeit moderate, situational setups for our infield starters. It is important to note that our entire roster relies on \"Lineup Pending\" status; should any confirmed lineups shift our hitters into lower-order roles, particularly for **Sam Antonacci** or **Wade Meckler**, we will lose the projected order-based bonuses that currently keep them in the starting mix. Furthermore, managers should keep a close eye on **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages**, as both are staring down Logan Henderson (2.84 xERA); their scores are tempered by the high risk posed by such a skilled opposing pitcher, even if their base projections remain respectably baseline.",
